{{!-- A1, "editorial rows", on the Tags Directory: one row per subject, name and description
against a post count.

	{{> "directory/tag-rows" tags=tags}}

	tags   the rows to render — the Directory partial owns the query

No image in this layout even though every tag may carry one; the design keeps the row
typographic and saves the photograph for the card layout. A tag with no description renders its
name and count and nothing else, which is a shorter row rather than a hole.

FULL PAGE WIDTH, not the design's 1120px column. The design insets this list inside the intro
above it, which reads as two pages: the eyebrow, the heading and the lead sentence start at the
page's left edge and every subject starts 90px to the right of them. The rows are the Surface's
content, the same way the Feed's cards are, and the Feed draws them at page width — so the
`--container-max` override is gone and this list lines up with the intro above it.

THE TOP RULE IS ON THE INNER DIV, NOT ON THE `container`. A border draws on the border box, so a
`border-t` on the container spanned the full 1320px while every row's `border-b` — set on an
`article` inside the container's padding — spanned 1256px, and the list opened with a rule 32px
wider at each end than the rules under it. One wrapper puts all fifteen rules on the same box.
A negative margin on the row would not have fixed it: the rule belongs to the `article`, and
`-mx-2` on the `<a>` inside it moves text, never the border it sits under. --}}
<section
	id="tags"
	aria-label="{{t "Tag directory"}}"
	class="container pt-16">
	<div class="border-border border-t">
		{{#foreach tags}}
			<article class="border-border border-b">
				<a
					href="{{url}}"
					class="text-text hover:bg-surface-2 grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] items-baseline gap-8 px-2 py-[30px] no-underline">
					<div>
						<h2 class="font-display tracking-heading text-[32px] leading-[1.16] font-medium">{{name}}</h2>

						{{#if description}}
							<p class="text-small text-muted mt-2.5 max-w-[64ch] leading-[1.6] text-pretty">{{description}}</p>
						{{/if}}
					</div>

					<span
						class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted whitespace-nowrap uppercase">{{plural count.posts empty=(t "No posts") singular=(t "% post") plural=(t "% posts")}}</span>
				</a>
			</article>
		{{/foreach}}
	</div>
</section>
